WEBVTT

00:00.041 --> 00:01.862
- [Voiceover] So, let's
get even more practice

00:01.862 --> 00:03.603
solving some exponential equations,

00:03.603 --> 00:05.867
and I have two different
exponential equations here.

00:05.867 --> 00:07.550
And like always, pause the video

00:07.550 --> 00:11.288
and see if you can solve
for x in both of them.

00:11.288 --> 00:13.889
All right, let's tackle
this one in purple first.

00:13.889 --> 00:16.239
And you might first notice that

00:16.239 --> 00:19.264
on both sides of the equation
I have different bases.

00:19.264 --> 00:21.562
So, it would be nice
to have a common base.

00:21.562 --> 00:22.967
And when you look at it, you're like,

00:22.967 --> 00:25.161
"Well, 32 is not a power of eight,

00:25.161 --> 00:27.483
"or at least it's not an
integer power of eight."

00:27.483 --> 00:30.652
But, they are both powers of two.

00:30.652 --> 00:35.017
32 is the same thing as
two to the fifth power,

00:35.017 --> 00:36.236
two to the fifth power,

00:36.236 --> 00:40.653
and eight is the same thing
as two to the third power,

00:40.653 --> 00:41.669
two to the third power.

00:41.669 --> 00:44.119
So, I can rewrite our original equation,

00:44.119 --> 00:46.255
as, instead of writing
32, I could write it

00:46.255 --> 00:48.911
as two to the fifth,

00:49.331 --> 00:50.620
and then that's going to be raised

00:50.620 --> 00:53.075
to the x over three power,

00:53.615 --> 00:55.112
X over three power,

00:55.112 --> 00:57.758
is equal to, instead of writing eight,

00:57.758 --> 01:00.347
I could write two to the third power,

01:00.347 --> 01:02.055
two to the third power,

01:02.055 --> 01:05.219
and I'm raising that to the x minus 12,

01:05.219 --> 01:07.267
x minus 12.

01:07.267 --> 01:08.718
Now if I raise something to a power,

01:08.718 --> 01:09.972
and then raise that to a power,

01:09.972 --> 01:12.154
I could just multiply these exponents.

01:12.154 --> 01:16.257
So, I can rewrite the
left-hand side as two

01:16.257 --> 01:20.675
to the five-x over three,

01:20.675 --> 01:23.612
five-x over three power.

01:23.612 --> 01:25.365
I just multiply these exponents.

01:25.365 --> 01:27.827
And that's going to be equal to

01:27.827 --> 01:29.916
two to the...

01:29.916 --> 01:34.856
And now I just multiply
the three times x minus 12.

01:34.856 --> 01:39.062
So, two to the three-x minus 36,

01:39.062 --> 01:40.746
and now things have simplified nicely.

01:40.746 --> 01:42.959
I have two to this power is equal to

01:42.959 --> 01:44.491
two to that power.

01:44.491 --> 01:47.343
So, these two exponents
must be equal to each other.

01:47.343 --> 01:50.827
Five-x over three must be equal to

01:50.827 --> 01:53.406
three-x minus 36.

01:53.406 --> 01:56.293
So, let's set them equal to
each other and solve for x.

01:56.299 --> 02:00.555
So five-x over three is equal to

02:00.555 --> 02:03.780
three-x minus 36.

02:03.780 --> 02:05.680
Let's see, we could,

02:05.680 --> 02:08.989
we could multiply, we could multiply

02:08.989 --> 02:11.439
everything by three.

02:11.439 --> 02:12.904
Let's do that.

02:12.904 --> 02:15.911
So if we multiply everything times three,

02:15.911 --> 02:19.371
here we're going to get five-x

02:19.371 --> 02:24.331
is equal to nine-x minus...

02:24.331 --> 02:24.908
What is this?

02:24.908 --> 02:27.648
Nine-x minus 108.

02:27.648 --> 02:31.049
And now we can subtract nine-x

02:31.049 --> 02:32.442
from both sides,

02:32.442 --> 02:34.787
and so we will get five-x minus nine-x

02:34.787 --> 02:37.938
is gonna be negative four-x is equal to

02:37.938 --> 02:40.260
negative 108.

02:40.260 --> 02:41.514
We're in the homestretch here.

02:41.514 --> 02:43.928
Divide, whoops, sorry about that.

02:43.928 --> 02:47.250
We could divide both
sides by negative four.

02:47.690 --> 02:49.210
Negative four.

02:49.210 --> 02:51.776
And we are left with x is equal to,

02:51.776 --> 02:53.773
what is this going to be, 27.

02:53.773 --> 02:56.095
X is equal to 27.

02:56.095 --> 02:58.869
And we are all done.

02:58.869 --> 02:59.811
We're all done.

02:59.811 --> 03:01.829
And if you had substituted
x back in there,

03:01.829 --> 03:04.786
you would get 32 to the 27 divided by 3,

03:04.786 --> 03:07.807
so 32 to the ninth
power, is the same thing

03:07.807 --> 03:11.674
as eight to the 27 minus 12th power.

03:11.674 --> 03:13.943
So eight to the 15th.

03:13.943 --> 03:16.871
Yeah, 27 minus 12,
eight to the 15th power.

03:16.871 --> 03:19.147
So, anyway, that was fun.

03:19.147 --> 03:21.473
Let's do the next one now.

03:21.473 --> 03:24.382
So this one looks
interesting in other ways.

03:24.382 --> 03:26.215
We have rational expressions.

03:26.215 --> 03:28.881
We have an exponential up
here, exponential down here.

03:28.881 --> 03:31.051
And the key realization here is...

03:31.051 --> 03:32.822
Well, the first thing I'd like to do.

03:32.822 --> 03:36.444
Let me write this 25 in terms of five.

03:36.444 --> 03:39.567
We know that 25 is the
same thing as five-squared.

03:39.567 --> 03:42.062
So, we can rewrite this as

03:42.872 --> 03:46.658
five to the four-x plus three

03:46.658 --> 03:49.864
over, instead of 25, I could rewrite that

03:49.864 --> 03:53.010
as five-squared, and then I'm gonna raise

03:53.010 --> 03:55.425
that to the nine minus x,

03:55.425 --> 03:58.222
to the nine minus x,

03:58.222 --> 03:59.546
and that, of course,
is going to be equal to

03:59.546 --> 04:03.087
five to the two-x plus five.

04:03.087 --> 04:04.944
Now five to the second, and then that

04:04.944 --> 04:06.662
to the nine minus x.

04:06.662 --> 04:08.880
I can just multiply these exponents.

04:08.880 --> 04:13.832
So, this is going to be five
to the four-x plus three

04:13.832 --> 04:18.068
over five to the...

04:18.068 --> 04:20.047
Two times nine is 18,

04:20.047 --> 04:23.704
two times negative-x is negative two-x,

04:23.704 --> 04:26.467
and that is going to be equal to,

04:26.467 --> 04:30.728
that is going to be equal to five

04:30.728 --> 04:34.048
to the two-x plus five.

04:34.048 --> 04:35.278
And now, let's see.

04:35.278 --> 04:37.147
There's multiple ways
that we could tackle it.

04:37.147 --> 04:39.254
We could multiply both
sides of this equation

04:39.254 --> 04:43.786
by five to the 18

04:43.786 --> 04:44.856
minus two-x.

04:44.856 --> 04:46.173
That's one way to do it.

04:46.173 --> 04:47.775
Or we could say, "Hey, look I have five

04:47.775 --> 04:49.353
"to some exponent divided by five

04:49.353 --> 04:51.687
"to some other exponent,
so I could just subtract

04:51.687 --> 04:54.589
"this blue exponent from this yellow one."

04:54.589 --> 04:57.223
So, the left-hand side will simplify to

04:57.793 --> 05:01.996
five to the four-x plus three

05:01.996 --> 05:06.430
minus, let me just do
minus in a neutral color,

05:06.430 --> 05:11.155
minus 18 minus two-x.

05:11.155 --> 05:13.210
18 minus two-x.

05:13.210 --> 05:15.648
and that, of course,
is going to be equal to

05:15.648 --> 05:17.505
what we've had on the right-hand side,

05:17.505 --> 05:20.849
five to the two-x plus five.

05:20.849 --> 05:23.554
Now we just have to simplify a little bit.

05:23.554 --> 05:25.574
Let's see, this is going to be...

05:25.574 --> 05:27.106
In fact, we could just say, "Look..."

05:27.106 --> 05:29.428
Now I'm having trouble
with my little pen tool.

05:29.428 --> 05:30.902
Whoops.

05:30.902 --> 05:31.773
All right.

05:31.773 --> 05:33.247
So now we could say this exponent needs

05:33.247 --> 05:34.269
to be equal to that exponent

05:34.269 --> 05:35.906
because we have the same base.

05:35.906 --> 05:40.182
And so, what we have here
on the left-hand side,

05:40.932 --> 05:44.891
that I could rewrite as four-x plus three

05:44.891 --> 05:48.792
minus 18 plus two-x.

05:48.792 --> 05:50.185
I'm just multiplying the negative times

05:50.185 --> 05:51.311
both of these terms.

05:51.311 --> 05:54.701
So, plus two-x, is going to be equal to

05:54.701 --> 05:56.929
two-x plus five.

05:56.929 --> 05:59.720
Two-x plus five.

05:59.720 --> 06:01.730
So, there's a bunch of different
things we could do here.

06:01.730 --> 06:04.766
One, we could subtract
two-x from both sides,

06:04.766 --> 06:06.205
that'll clean it up a little bit.

06:06.205 --> 06:07.749
Two-x from both sides.

06:07.749 --> 06:11.583
We could also subtract
five from both sides.

06:11.583 --> 06:13.345
So, let's just do that.

06:13.345 --> 06:17.083
So, well, let me just subtract it.

06:17.083 --> 06:19.265
Subtract five from both sides.

06:19.265 --> 06:20.821
I'm skipping some steps here,

06:20.821 --> 06:23.119
but I figure you're at this point

06:23.119 --> 06:25.956
reasonably comfortable
with linear equations.

06:25.956 --> 06:29.168
So then, on the left-hand side,

06:29.168 --> 06:31.722
we are going to have four-x,

06:31.722 --> 06:35.019
and then you have three
minus 18 minus five.

06:35.019 --> 06:39.296
Three minus 18 is negative 15,

06:39.296 --> 06:42.437
minus five, is negative 20,

06:42.437 --> 06:46.303
Is going to be equal to zero.

06:46.303 --> 06:48.462
And then, because those cancel out.

06:48.462 --> 06:49.843
And so add 20 to both sides,

06:49.843 --> 06:53.036
you get four-x is equal to 20.

06:53.036 --> 06:55.659
Divide both sides by four,

06:55.659 --> 06:58.724
and we get x is equal to five.

06:58.724 --> 07:00.846
And we are all done.
